      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by _the limit of the events-broker batching of messages for acking_? Do you mean Kafka\u0027s `max.poll.records`, or another batching limit?\n\nAs per the events-broker API, acks are not _batched_, an `ack()` call commits that offset immediately, so when the interval is due, we ack the latest event up to that point. I don\u0027t see any specific problem with that.\n\nHaving said that, there is a related problem in `events-kafka`, where those intermediate records remain in `ackRecords` (in `events-kafka`, or `events-kinesis`, for example). This is tracked by [515709509](https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/515709509).\n\n@ponch78@gmail.com, @luca.milanesio@gmail.com\nDo you think we should fix that before merging this change?",
      "parentUuid": "4fdbd9bc_9b017c42",
